\title{Data-Driven Streamflow Forecasting for the River Wensum:\newline A Pilot Study for the Upper Catchment}
\author{H.~Meadows, D.~Osei, and K.~Albrecht}
\date{April 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
The upper Wensum catchment floods the mill race at Fakenham two or three times each decade.
The Environment Agency maintains six gauging stations along the main stem and its tributaries.
This pilot study compares published modelling approaches before committing to an operational chain.

\section{Pilot Scope}
The pilot covers the 380~km$^{2}$ catchment above the Fakenham gauge.
Daily records from 2005 to 2024 form the training archive.
The findings below draw only on published evidence; no new model runs are reported here.

